sieve-filter-v2
; Word cost: each letter costs -log2 of its probability after the letter before (or after a
; word's start), and a word's end costs the same after its last letter, in quarter-bits
; rounded up, from a letter-pair model of the list. A word fails when some stretch of it
; costs more than `rate` per letter plus `slack`: kept as a leaky bucket, e = max(0, e +
; cost - rate), which must never pass slack. The countable stand-in for
; model-information-v1, with no dictionary of whole words. Measured on the lists (words
; of 3 to 9 random letters for noise), the defaults keep 99.7% of scowl-en-35's words
; and 98.8% of scowl-en-80-names', and 19% of random words.
; Generated by tools/build_text_plugins.py from scowl-2020.12.07-en-80-names.txt (sha256 d4aece883446c883591ad8c47ef265af945497fa4105aef6ccc30fd7dbfe2cba).
id        word-cost
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     text
symbols   lower27
describe  No stretch of a word costs more than the budget under a letter-pair model of the list.
param     rate   int  16  4  64  the cost allowed per letter, in quarter-bits (16 is 4 bits)
param     slack  int  40  0  200  how far over the rate a stretch may run, in quarter-bits

states    {2 + 26 * (slack + 1)}
start     0
accept    0..{1 + 26 * (slack + 1)}
t 0 " " 1
t 1 " " 1
t 0 "a" {2 + 0 * (slack + 1)}
if {max(0, 17 - rate) <= slack}
